# Native FP16 reference: kernels exist, full-graph contracts remain unvalidated

The pinned original DLL contains genuine FP16 implementations of every major
network stage. A native FP16 trunk is therefore plausible on SM120, but it is
not ready to benchmark: only ordinary C32/C64/C128/C256 blocks have bounded
native parity evidence. C512, global attention, resolution transitions and
renderer endpoints still require their own Half layouts, records and launch
protocols. The completed 931-geometry native comparison is **FP8 blocks 1–69**;
it provides no native FP16 speed or full-graph parity result.

This is a CPU-only audit. It reread the original PE resources, verified all
seven extracted PTX/cubin hashes and checked every non-FP8 entry against cached
SASS. It did not import Torch, execute CUDA or change an active source file.
[The reproducible evidence](../outputs/v35-native-fp16-feasibility/evidence.json.draft)
records every symbol, source line, parameter size, asset hash and runtime report
used below.

## What is present in the original binary

Original DLL SHA256:
`e16bcf15e16e13f527491cdf7845b2fe6521a738d8f7c9c721866a8496e1fc8e`.
All seven extracted NR modules target **SM120, PTX 9.4**. They contain 109
non-FP8 entrypoints with actual
`mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k16.row.col.f16.f16.f16.f16`, plus two repacks and a
counter-clear utility. All 112 names occur in cached original SASS.

The table lists ordinary entry names; the evidence also preserves the exact
wait, chained, tilesync and view variants. A matching name or argument-record
size does not establish a safe launch configuration.

| Graph role | Original FP16 entry / PTX location | Argument bytes | Current contract evidence |
|---|---|---:|---|
| Block 0, adapter and initial block/downsample | `cc_tinlayout_fused_pre_block_swin_1h_32_1` and `_ds`; [module 0](../assets/vendor_modules/module_0.ptx), lines 21 / 29454 | 264 | Symbols only for FP16; textures, conditioning and derived pre-record unmapped |
| C32, blocks 1–4 and 66–69 | `cc_tinlayout_fused_swin_1h_32_1`; module 0:228944; `_inpview`, `_outview`, `_ds`, `_upsample` also present | 96 | Ordinary block bounded parity; transition/view variants unvalidated |
| C64, blocks 5–8 / 62–65 | `cc_tinlayout_fused_swin_2h_64_2`; [module 1](../assets/vendor_modules/module_1.ptx):41; same four view/transition suffixes | 88 | Ordinary block bounded parity |
| C128, blocks 9–14 / 56–61 | `cc_tinlayout_fused_swin_4h_128_4`; [module 2](../assets/vendor_modules/module_2.ptx):41; same suffixes | 88 | Ordinary block bounded parity |
| C256, blocks 15–22 / 48–55 | `cc_tinlayout_fused_swin_8h_256_8`; [module 3](../assets/vendor_modules/module_3.ptx):41; same suffixes | 88 | Ordinary block bounded parity |
| C512, blocks 23–30 / 40–47 | `cc_split_swin_16h_ffwd_512`, `ffwd_proj_512`, `qkv_512`, `proj_512`; [module 4](../assets/vendor_modules/module_4.ptx):109 / 43051 / 87243 / 119676 | 56 / 72 / 56 / 72 | Four-stage FP16 buffers, branch records and launches unvalidated; input/output views exist |
| Block 30 downsample/head | `cc_split_swin_16h_proj_pool_512`, `cc_split_swin_16h_final_head_512`; module 4:155736 / 176244 | 80 / 40 | Half pool/head storage and padded transitions unvalidated |
| Global blocks 31–38 | `cc_vit_1d_ffn_expand`, `ffn_contract`, `qkv`, `attention`, `projection`; [module 5](../assets/vendor_modules/module_5.ptx):167633 / 192448 / 213677 / 239908 / 256974 | 72 / 72 / 80 / 64 / 72 | FP16 arithmetic exists; partition/completion ABI and whole-block parity unvalidated |
| Spatial/token bridges | `cc_vit_1d_repack_2d_to_1d`, `cc_vit_1d_repack_1d_to_2d`; module 5:166989 / 167359 | 24 | Half token/image layout and padding unvalidated |
| Block 39 upsample/projection | `cc_dec_input_upsample_1024_512`; [module 6](../assets/vendor_modules/module_6.ptx):25 | 80 | Half split projection, skip, counters and cropped target contract unvalidated |
