These are original **SM120** kernels, not a runnable unchanged native reference
for RTX 30-series SM86 or SM80. Candidate FP16 compilation/support on SM80+
remains a separate claim. Retargeting this PTX would create a rebuilt reference,
not establish original-DLL speed on those devices. This audit covers the seven
NR bundles, not the eight older utility bundles excluded during extraction.

## Weights and arithmetic

The PE contains one 147,695,410-byte `10/WEIGHTS_HT/1033` resource and a version
resource. Its recovered checkpoint has 153 records across 11 stages. Most
learned matrices are packed E4M3; the 16→32 input adapter and 32→4 head already
store Half matrices. There is no separately identified FP16 checkpoint or
verified DLL-host conversion routine.

Finite decoded E4 values are exactly representable in Half. Existing probes
derive native Half records from those same learned values, repack matrices to
K16/N16 fragments, preserve Half scales/biases and float head scales, and use
the original FP16 record offsets. Ordinary C32 grows from 20,672 to 32,960
bytes; derived C64/C128/C256 allocations are 106,816 / 361,024 / 1,311,808 bytes.
This is a reference with **derived Half records**, not recovered higher-
precision trained weights. Transition, C512, global, pre and post records
still need equivalent offset/read-coverage proofs.

Half activation storage also has a different fragment map: each 4×4 image
tile has 512 bytes per 16-channel plane. Doubling FP8 offsets is not a valid
layout conversion. The ordinary address proofs cover this map, actual reads
and stores, alignment, guarded bounds and shared-memory epochs.

The candidate's FP16 mode keeps intermediate publications in Half, whereas
FP8 mode rounds them to E4M3. That is a real network-arithmetic distinction.
The original ordinary-block tests support the Half mode in their tested
scope. The [normalization SASS audit](native-fp16-arithmetic-audit.md.draft)
and [global Q/K trace](fp16-global-norm-sass-trace.md.draft) confirm that the
separate-looking PTX squares compile to the existing Half multiply/FMA tree;
they do not justify an alternative normalizer or prove the global launch ABI.

The main protocol risk is visible in original global FP16 code. Its contraction
and projection issue `red.global.v4.f16x2.add.noftz` into Half output after
the initial partition stores, with completion polling. Their parameter reads
do not consume the FP8 scratch pointer used by the current helper. QKV also
differs from the FP8 scratch contract. Partition order, seed placement,
initialization, counters, visibility, tail storage and forward progress must
be recovered and tested; the presence of reductions alone proves neither
ordered equivalence nor nondeterminism.

## What has actually run

| Saved native FP16 proof | Cases and shapes | Result and limits |
|---|---|---|
| [C32 v24](../outputs/vendor_fp16_c32_v24.json) | 16 cases, 16×24; four fixtures × four phases, real block 1 included | Byte-exact; 48 ordinary + 48 poisoned graph replays; memcheck zero errors |
| [Wider encoder v28](../outputs/vendor_fp16_window_v28_retry.json) | 48 cases, 8×8; blocks 5/9/15, four fixtures × four phases | Byte-exact; 144 + 144 replays; memcheck zero errors |
| [Wider decoder v28](../outputs/vendor_fp16_window_v28_decoder.json) | 48 cases, 12×20; ordinary blocks 63/57/49, same fixtures/phases | Byte-exact; 144 + 144 replays; memcheck zero errors; **not** an upsample/transition test |
| [Wider racecheck v28](../outputs/vendor_fp16_window_v28_race_corrected.json) | 12 real-weight cases, 8×8, blocks 5/9/15 × four phases | Byte-exact; 36 + 36 replays; zero hazards/errors/warnings |

Every report checks supplied inputs/weights and allocation guards. Candidate
outputs use extension allocations and retained byte comparisons, not external
red zones. The evidence pins the historical v24/v28 candidate hashes; these
are not fresh v35 validations. All four reports explicitly state
`native_speed=false`, `dll_host_executed=false` and
`dll_host_conversion_verified=false`. There is no native FP16 timing gate.

## Smallest honest path to a full reference

1. Add a separate FP16 contract path to the native helpers, leaving the FP8
   runner intact. Reuse pinned Driver API loading, guards, lifetime management,
   poisoned graphs and journal machinery. Derive and byte-verify Half records
   and layouts for each missing family before introducing its launch.
2. Validate C512 stages and each transition/view/repack independently, including
   padded extents used by `Geometry`. Then recover global FP16 partition and
   completion behavior with bounded guarded fixtures, repeated capture/replay
   and sanitizers. A matching Q/K norm is only one checkpoint in that proof.
3. Build a resident FP16 blocks 1–69 chain with Half skip/branch buffers, fresh
   boundary and repeat checks, and the exact original Half symbols. Measure
   matching physical Half endpoints and include candidate layout adapters.
   Reuse continuous geometry enumeration only after these contracts pass.
4. Treat 0–70/renderer coverage separately. FP16 pre0 requires the original
   texture/conditioning prefix and derived pre-record; post70 requires Half
   input/adapter layouts and the surface/blend contract. Existing FP8 feature
   instrumentation and the null-texture RGB+zero-alpha post probe do not
   establish general FP16 preprocessing, fourth neural logit or renderer
   composition. Never label an instrumented prefix as unchanged DLL execution.

The present `native_benchmark.py` rejects FP16, and `vendor_trunk.py`,
`vendor_global_block.py`, `vendor_window512_block.py` and `vendor_connectors.py`
hard-code FP8 symbols, byte allocations or scratch protocols. A suffix switch
is insufficient. Use the ordered extension as the candidate arithmetic
reference; its ordinary floating matmul reference backend is not an exact
native MMA oracle. No active harness changes are proposed in this audit.

Reproduce the CPU evidence from the project root:

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe outputs\v35-native-fp16-feasibility\inspect.py.draft
```

Evidence SHA256:
`aad45285b326461e2c0296545187d7f982a18f09ef38376a089999cee3c23f7c`.
The result establishes available code and bounded existing evidence. It does
not establish native FP16 trunk/full-graph parity, speed or an 85% roofline gate.
